import Vsa.Elf
import Vsa.Sim.StateNF

/-!
# Layer 0 — full GPR access battery (`rX_bits` / `wX_bits`) for x1..x31

Mechanical replication of the `Execute.lean` register-access characterizations
(`rX_bits_x10`, `wX_bits_x10`) across every general-purpose register index.
For each `i ∈ 1..31` this file provides:

* `rX_bits_x<i>` : reading `x<i>` returns the pinned value, touching no state;
* `wX_bits_x<i>` : writing `x<i>` inserts `d` into the register file.

plus `wX_bits_zero`, characterizing the `x0` write as a state-preserving no-op
(the `match` selects `pure ()` and the `r != 0` callback guard is false). The
`x0` *read* is `rX_bits_zero` in `Execute.lean` and is deliberately not
duplicated here.

The proofs are the identical single `simp only` per lemma used in `Execute.lean`:
the load-bearing move reduces the 32-way `match r with` on the concrete register
index (arriving as `Regno (BitVec.toNatInt i)`) down to its single reachable arm
via `Sail.BitVec.toNatInt, Int.ofNat_eq_natCast, Int.toNat_natCast,
BitVec.reduceToNat`, after which iota-reduction picks the arm.

## ABI name ↔ register index (for downstream readability)

| ABI   | reg | ABI   | reg | ABI   | reg | ABI   | reg |
|-------|-----|-------|-----|-------|-----|-------|-----|
| ra    | x1  | t2    | x7  | a5    | x15 | s7    | x23 |
| sp    | x2  | s0/fp | x8  | a6    | x16 | s8    | x24 |
| gp    | x3  | s1    | x9  | a7    | x17 | s9    | x25 |
| tp    | x4  | a0    | x10 | s2    | x18 | s10   | x26 |
| t0    | x5  | a1    | x11 | s3    | x19 | s11   | x27 |
| t1    | x6  | a2    | x12 | s4    | x20 | t3    | x28 |
|       |     | a3    | x13 | s5    | x21 | t4    | x29 |
|       |     | a4    | x14 | s6    | x22 | t5    | x30 |
|       |     |       |     |       |     | t6    | x31 |

(`x0` = `zero`, hardwired to the constant `0`.)

Generated by a Python heredoc emitting this Lean text (see the M2 task record);
the per-lemma proof scripts are hand-validated copies of the `Execute.lean`
shapes.
-/

open LeanRV64DExecutable LeanRV64DExecutable.Functions Sail ConcurrencyInterfaceV1 Vsa
open Register

set_option maxHeartbeats 8000000
set_option maxRecDepth 1000000

namespace Vsa.Sim

/-- `x0` write is a no-op: the `match` selects `pure ()` and the `r != 0`
write-callback guard is false, so the state is returned unchanged. -/
theorem wX_bits_zero (σ : SequentialState RegisterType trivialChoiceSource)
    (d : BitVec 64) :
    (wX_bits (regidx.Regidx 0x00#5) d).run σ = .ok () σ := by
  simp only [wX_bits, wX, bind, EStateM.bind, pure, EStateM.pure,
    EStateM.run, Sail.BitVec.toNatInt,
    Int.ofNat_eq_natCast, Int.toNat_natCast, BitVec.reduceToNat,
    bne_self_eq_false, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]

